{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/901541-what-media-is-comfort-food-for-you","id":901541,"title":"What media is \"comfort food\" for you?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T17:20:15-07:00","id":901541,"title":"What media is \"comfort food\" for you?","content":"When you're mentally or emotionally worn, what sorts of media (general, or specific, games count) help you feel a bit better, or at least keep you on an even keel?<br /> <br /> For me, a<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">s a general rule, romantic anime/manga. First Person Shooters (because </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">while they can require physical mastery, they don't require or inspire deep </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">emotions, so they let me recharge), ummm oh, and The Crow. I just like it.\ufeff</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:36:40-07:00","id":901560,"title":"","content":"Books and documentaries. <br /> <br /> Specifically, I read Anne McCaffrey Dragonriders of Pern or watch Cosmos. <br /> <br /> When I was at a really low point, I watched Babylon 5. At the time I really identified with Garibaldi when he was programed by Bester. That scene where Bester releases him gets me every time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:49:34-07:00","id":901580,"title":"","content":"Comfy, light-hearted shows where I don't have to think much about things. Comedic LPs and other such stuff. Browsing for nice character or setting art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:48:56-07:00","id":902516,"title":"","content":"Music, NPC/Character building, and stand up comedy generally help me. If I am in a pissy mood, FPS help. I also really like watching vogue dancing videos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Debating between ghouls and hunters PbP","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11874-melora","name":"Melora","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:54:54-07:00","id":902648,"title":"","content":"Because of it invariably being frustration or anger that leads to me feeling worn, my go-to remedy is heavy metal - especially if I'm able to 'sing' along, jam it out on my own guitar, or demolish something while I listen to it (though I mean productive demolition such as tearing down a condemned structure or chopping firewood, not destruction for its own sake).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:28:17-07:00","id":902736,"title":"","content":"Shaw brother Kung Fu films with bad dubbing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:32:20-07:00","id":902839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/901541-what-media-is-comfort-food-for-you?p=902648#post902648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of it invariably being frustration or anger that leads to me feeling worn, my go-to remedy is heavy metal - especially if I'm able to 'sing' along, jam it out on my own guitar, or demolish something while I listen to it (though I mean productive demolition such as tearing down a condemned structure or chopping firewood, not destruction for its own sake).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, metal for me too, but not JUST heavy. And to everyone, thanks for sharing, feel free to keep them coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T04:58:57-07:00","id":903398,"title":"","content":"I have a certain fondness for bad conspiracy documentaries (even put them on when I do the dishes or clean my appartment), so that's a good way to cheer me up when I'm feeling down. I have a fondness for certain cartoons, even &quot;children&quot; cartoons (A:tLA, Rick and Morty, Archer, Gravity Falls), that I tend to binge on when alone and not in a particularily productive mood.<br /> <br /> I don't have confort books. I love reading, but it's usually something I do when I'm already feeling ok. Huh. I never noticed that before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T04:34:59-07:00","id":904083,"title":"","content":"Video games...Mostly Skyrim or Fallout, something that gives me as much escapism as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:19:23-07:00","id":905275,"title":"","content":"tabletop rpg's, that's why Im here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:20:51-07:00","id":905469,"title":"","content":"Cloud Atlas, I just love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T20:40:41-07:00","id":908078,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I like <b>Say Yes to the Dress</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T20:58:08-07:00","id":908090,"title":"","content":"Police procedural shows. CSI, NCIS, Criminal minds, law &amp; Order anything with a dead body, barely any caracterization and a poor understanding of police procedure and forensic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:40:23-07:00","id":928116,"title":"","content":"*Bump*<br /> <br /> Star Wars is my comfort franchise. It grabbed my imagination and never let go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:11:59-07:00","id":928144,"title":"","content":"Slow-paced anime is great when I'm emotionally drained. I discovered Holic at a time when I was under a lot of stress and it was just a total life saver for me, still my favorite anime. Mushi Shi is another good one, though it sometimes puts me to sleep. Familiar video games, which mostly means what ever I'm playing most at that specific time. Some of my childhood favorite movies are good for when adult life gets too stressful. Labyrinth. Princess Bride. The Last Unicorn.<br /> <br /> Every time I get sick enough that I have to take off work, I get a quart of chicken noodle soup from the nearby Jewish deli (best soup I have ever had!) and watch The 10th Kingdom. It's like 8 hours long, I could probably recite the script from memory almost verbatim at this point, and it's perfect for killing days when I can't get out of bed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:08:14-07:00","id":928187,"title":"","content":"Video games usually. Something slow-paced but that requires thought, but not tactical rpgs or anything like that. FPSes are good, but they can't be twi